    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.Intro">A profile is a complete setup: where thumbnails sit, hotkeys, colours, crops and client layout. Keep one per activity, like mining and PvP.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Title">Working with profiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.profiles.Body">- **New** starts an empty profile and switches to it.&#x0A;- **Copy** copies one profile into another: everything, or only thumbnail positions.&#x0A;- **Delete** removes the current profile for good. You always keep at least one.&#x0A;&#x0A;You can also switch from the profile menu at the top left, or with the profile hotkeys.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Title">Backups and moving to another PC</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.app.profiles.backups.Body">**Back up now** saves a dated copy in the Backups folder. MultiPreview also keeps a copy when it starts, if your settings changed since the last one (the last 10), and one before every update. If your settings file can't be read or is missing, it offers these copies when it starts.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Export** saves your settings file wherever you like. **Import** replaces all your settings with an exported file. Your current settings are backed up first, and MultiPreview needs a restart to use the imported ones everywhere.&#x0A;&#x0A;Your settings are normally kept in %APPDATA%\EVE MultiPreview. To keep them beside MultiPreview.exe instead (a portable install), close MultiPreview, copy your settings file there, and put an empty file named portable.txt beside the exe.</sys:String>
