    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Groups.DeleteBoth">Delete the group '{0}'?&#x0A;&#x0A;Delete everywhere: its colour goes from every profile, and its keys and order from this profile.&#x0A;Only this profile's keys: the keys and order go, and the colour group stays.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Groups.DeleteColour">Delete the group '{0}'? Its colour goes from every profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Groups.DeleteKeys">Delete the group '{0}' from this profile?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.groups.Intro">A group is a set of characters with a shared border colour and its own next and previous keys. Use one for a fleet, a mining crew or your scouts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.groups.keys.Title">Switching inside a group</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.groups.keys.Body">**Next client** and **Previous client** switch between the group's members in the order shown. Drag a name onto another to move it there, or onto empty space to move it last.&#x0A;&#x0A;A character can be in several groups. Groups that share a next key take turns as one list.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.groups.scope.Title">Colours and profiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.groups.scope.Body">A group's **colour** applies in every profile. Its **keys** and **order** belong to the current profile, so each profile can switch differently.&#x0A;&#x0A;Turn on **Show group borders** to paint every member's thumbnail in its group colour.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Delete** asks whether to remove the whole group, colour included, or only this profile's keys and order.</sys:String>
