    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.Intro">Everything MultiPreview keeps for this character, in one place. Changes apply to the current profile unless a card says otherwise.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.switching.Title">Switching to this character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.switching.Body">The **hotkey** switches straight to this character. Give the same key to two characters and it switches between them.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Include in cycling** decides whether the next and previous client keys stop here. It resets when MultiPreview restarts.&#x0A;&#x0A;Groups are edited on the **Groups** page, where you also set their keys and order.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.thumbnail.Title">This character's thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.thumbnail.Body">- **Label** adds your own text, like Scout. Its colour and size can differ from the other text.&#x0A;- **Own size** gives this thumbnail its own width and height. A character needs to have been logged in once in this profile.&#x0A;- **Second thumbnail** adds a separate picture-in-picture view of the same client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.colors.Title">Colours</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.colors.Body">These colours are used only while **Use per-character colours** is on for the profile (Clients › Characters).&#x0A;- The two border colours mark this character's thumbnail when it is the client you're playing and when it isn't.&#x0A;- **Text colour** colours the text on its thumbnail. Until you pick one, it follows Thumbnails › Text &amp; borders.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Reset colours** goes back to the colours every character uses.</sys:String>
