    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.character.remove">Forget</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.forgetRow">Forget this character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.forgetRow.Desc">Removes its hotkey, colours, label, size, crops and every other setting, in every profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.character.forget">Forget…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Character.ForgetTitle">Forget character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Character.ForgetConfirm">Forget '{0}'? Its settings are removed from every profile and from its groups and slots. This can't be undone. If the client is running, it stays on the list with default settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Character.Forgotten">'{0}' forgotten.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.clients.Title">Client window, CPU and sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.clients.Body">- **Never minimize** keeps this client open when the others are minimized on a switch.&#x0A;- **CPU core in the background** pins the client to one core while it isn't the one you're playing, if background priority is managed.&#x0A;- **Game volume** sets this client's volume in Windows. It's remembered for next time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.stats.Title">Stats overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.stats.Body">The stats overlay shows numbers such as damage per second or ISK per hour next to a thumbnail. **Default** uses the numbers chosen for every character. **On** or **Off** shows or hides a whole group for this character only.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.crops.Title">Crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.crops.Body">A crop window shows one part of this client, such as its overview, in its own small window. Crop windows are edited on the Crop windows page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.remove.Title">Forgetting a character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.character.remove.Body">**Forget** removes everything MultiPreview keeps for this character, in every profile: hotkey, colours, label, size, second thumbnail, crops, sound and its place in groups and slots. Use it for a character you no longer play. It asks first and can't be undone.</sys:String>
    <!-- Clients › Hotkeys &amp; switching -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.hotkeys">Hotkeys &amp; switching</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.hotkeys.Desc">Keys that switch clients or control MultiPreview, and how they behave.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Unit.Ms">ms</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Filter.Sounds">Sound files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.hotkeys.behaviour">How hotkeys behave</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.scope">Hotkeys work</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.scope.Desc">Only while EVE is in front leaves your keys alone in other apps.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.ScopeEverywhere">Everywhere</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.ScopeEve">Only while EVE is in front</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.wildcard">Hotkeys work while Ctrl, Shift or Alt is held</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.wildcard.Desc">On: holding Ctrl to lock targets doesn't stop your hotkeys. Off: a one-key hotkey like V fires only on its own, so Ctrl+V still pastes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideKeystrokes">Hide hotkeys from EVE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideKeystrokes.Desc">The client you switch to never sees the hotkey. Off: it gets the key's release, which can make your first click only focus the overview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.carryModifiers">Carry held Ctrl, Shift and Alt to the next client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.carryModifiers.Desc">Keeps holding Ctrl to lock working after a switch. Turn it off if locking stops working after you switch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.carryKeys">Carry other held keys to the next client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.carryKeys.Desc">Hold F1 and cycle to press it on each client. Turn it off if a module key you haven't released yet fires on the next client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideHeld">Hide still-held keys from the next client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideHeld.Desc">A key still down when you switch is kept from the client you land on until you let go, so holding A or S can't make it align or warp. Wins over the option above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.broadcastHud">Show which held key is carried</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.broadcastHud.Desc">A small on-screen pill. Drag it where you like.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.hotkeys.cycling">Switching between clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleNext">Next client, all running clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleNext.Desc">Switches to the next running client, whatever its group.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cyclePrevious">Previous client, all running clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleWhileHeld">Keep switching while the key is held</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleWhileHeld.Desc">Off: each press switches exactly one client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleDelay">Time between switches while held</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.cycleDelay.Desc">Lower is faster. 100 ms is the default.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.wrapSound">Play a sound when switching wraps around</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.wrapSound.Desc">Tells you you're back at the first client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.wrapSoundFile">Wrap-around sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.includeLogins">Include clients at the login screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.includeLogins.Desc">The next and previous client keys also stop at clients that haven't picked a character yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.hotkeys.app">MultiPreview hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.suspend">Pause hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.suspend.Desc">Turns every other hotkey off and back on. This one keeps working while paused.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.clickThrough">Click-through thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.clickThrough.Desc">Clicks go through the thumbnails to whatever is behind them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideAll">Hide or show all thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideAll.Desc">Second thumbnails, stats overlays and crop windows too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hidePrimary">Hide or show the main thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hidePip">Hide or show second thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.hideCrops">Hide or show crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.quickSwitch">Quick-switch wheel</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.lockPositions">Lock or unlock thumbnail positions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.undo">Undo a layout change</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.undo.Desc">Avoid keys EVE uses, like Ctrl+Z.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.redo">Redo a layout change</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.profileNext">Next profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.profilePrevious">Previous profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.closeAll">Close all clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.closeAll.Desc">Ends every EVE client MultiPreview is tracking, after one confirmation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.hotkeys.check">Conflict check</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.conflicts">Keys used twice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.hotkeys.conflicts.Desc">Updates as you change keys. Characters that share a key on purpose aren't listed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Conflicts.None">No conflicts: every key does one thing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Conflicts.Count">{0} key(s) are used twice. Pick a different key for one of each pair.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.Intro">Keys that switch clients and control MultiPreview, and how they behave. The conflict check at the bottom shows keys that do two things.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.scope.Title">Where hotkeys work</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.scope.Body">**Everywhere** catches your hotkeys whatever app is in front, so a key pressed in a browser still switches clients. **Only while EVE is in front** leaves the keys alone in other apps.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Hotkeys work while Ctrl, Shift or Alt is held** matters if you hold Ctrl to lock targets. Turn it off if a one-key hotkey stops Ctrl+V or Ctrl+C reaching EVE.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Hide hotkeys from EVE** stops the client you switch to from seeing the key you pressed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.held.Title">Keys you're still holding</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.held.Body">When you switch while holding keys, MultiPreview can carry them to the next client or hide them from it.&#x0A;- **Carry Ctrl, Shift and Alt**: keep holding Ctrl to lock targets after a switch.&#x0A;- **Carry other held keys**: hold F1 and cycle to fire it on every client.&#x0A;- **Hide still-held keys**: holding A or S never makes the next client align or warp.&#x0A;&#x0A;The on-screen pill shows which key is being carried.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.cycling.Title">Next and previous client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.cycling.Body">**Next client** and **Previous client** go through every running client. Groups have their own keys on the Groups page.&#x0A;&#x0A;Hold the key to keep switching, at the time you set. Turn that off to switch exactly one client per press.&#x0A;&#x0A;A sound can tell you when you've gone round to the first client again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.app.Title">MultiPreview hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.app.Body">Keys for MultiPreview itself: pause every hotkey, make thumbnails click-through, hide them, lock their positions, undo a layout change, change profile, or close every client. Pick keys EVE doesn't use. **Pause hotkeys** keeps working while paused, so you can always turn them back on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.conflicts.Title">Keys used twice</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.hotkeys.conflicts.Body">When two things share a key, only one of them runs. The conflict check lists each pair; click one to change its key.&#x0A;&#x0A;Not listed, because they work on purpose: characters with the same key (the key switches between them), and groups with the same next key (they share one list).</sys:String>
    <!-- Clients › Windows & positions -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.windows">Windows &amp; positions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.windows.Desc">Minimizing the clients you leave, and where client windows go.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.windows.minimizing">Minimizing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.minimizeInactive">Minimize clients when you switch away</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.minimizeInactive.Desc">Minimized clients stop drawing, which saves a lot of GPU.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.minimizeDelay">Wait before minimizing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.neverMinimize">Never minimize</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.neverMinimize.Desc">These characters stay open when you switch away.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.neverMinimize.Empty">Nobody yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.NeverMinimize.Add">Add…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.NeverMinimize.AddTitle">Never minimize this character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.windows.placement">Window position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionMode">Where client windows go</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionMode.Desc">Applied when a client is found and each time you switch to it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.PositionOff">Where EVE puts them</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.PositionCenter">Centred on the monitor</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.PositionCustom">At a fixed X and Y</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.PositionSlots">In fixed slots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionX">X</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionX.Desc">From the left edge of the monitor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionY">Y</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.positionY.Desc">From the top edge of the monitor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.alwaysMaximize">Always maximize the client you switch to</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.trackPositions">Remember where each client window was</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.trackPositions.Desc">Puts each client back where you left it. While this is on, Centred and a fixed X and Y aren't used.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.coverTaskbar">Let the active client cover the taskbar</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.coverTaskbar.Desc">For windows as tall as the screen. The active client sits above the taskbar and drops behind it when you switch away. Centring also uses the whole screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.windows.slots">Fixed slots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.slots">Slots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.slots.Desc">Each slot is a place on a monitor. Listed characters go to their slot; everyone else goes to the default slot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.clients.windows.addSlot">Add slot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.clients.windows.snapNow">Snap clients now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.NoDefault">No default slot: only listed characters are moved</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Default">Default</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Monitor">Monitor</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.MonitorMissing">(not connected) {0} {1}×{2}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Primary">primary</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.ScaledShort">different scaling</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.X">X</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Y">Y</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.W">Width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.H">Height</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Capture">Copy from a client…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Fill">Fill the screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Delete">Delete…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.DeleteTitle">Delete slot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.DeleteConfirm">Delete the slot '{0}'? Its characters go to the default slot instead.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Characters">Characters</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.AddCharacter">Add…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.AddCharacterTitle">Send a character to '{0}'</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.NoClients">No logged-in clients are running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.CaptureFail">That client isn't in a normal window (it may be minimized or maximized). Restore it and try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.NoMonitor">Monitor not connected: this slot is skipped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.TooSmall">Too small: the minimum is 640×360. This slot is skipped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.NoFit">Doesn't fit the {0}×{1} monitor: this slot is skipped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.WhoDefault">Default slot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.Scaled">This monitor's Windows scaling differs from your primary's, so EVE's image is rescaled here. Positions are in MultiPreview's {0}×{1} units for this {2}×{3} monitor. For a pixel-exact client, give it the same scaling as your primary.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.neverMove">Never move</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.neverMove.Desc">These characters' windows are never moved or resized, even with a default slot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Slot.NeverMoveTitle">Never move this character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.slotsResize">Resize clients to their slot</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.slotsResize.Desc">Off: clients are only moved into place and keep their own size.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.windows.charSelect">Character select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.charSelectCycle">Switch between clients at character select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.charSelectCycle.Desc">Two extra keys for logging in many clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.charSelectNext">Next client at character select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.windows.charSelectPrevious">Previous client at character select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.Intro">How MultiPreview handles your EVE windows: minimizing the ones you leave, and where each window goes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.minimize.Title">Minimizing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.minimize.Body">**Minimize clients when you switch away** minimizes every other client when you switch, so only the one you play draws. That saves a lot of GPU with many clients.&#x0A;&#x0A;Characters on the **Never minimize** list stay open, for example a scout you keep an eye on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.position.Title">Where windows go</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.position.Body">MultiPreview can move each client when it's found and whenever you switch to it:&#x0A;- **Centred on the monitor**&#x0A;- **At a fixed X and Y**&#x0A;- **In fixed slots**: places on your monitors, one per character or shared.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Remember where each client window was** puts every client back where you left it instead.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.slots.Title">Fixed slots</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.slots.Body">A slot is a rectangle on one monitor. List characters in a slot to send them there; everyone else goes to the **default** slot, or stays put if there's none.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Copy from a client** takes a running client's current window. A slot must be at least 640×360 and fit its monitor, or it's skipped.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Snap clients now** moves every running client into its slot.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.charSelect.Title">Character select</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.windows.charSelect.Body">Turn this on for two keys that switch between clients still at the character select screen, handy when logging in many clients one after another.</sys:String>

    <!-- Clients › Game audio -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.audio">Game audio</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.clients.audio.Desc">Hear only the client you're playing, and set each client's volume.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.audio.solo">Active client only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.autoSolo">Only hear the active client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.autoSolo.Desc">When you switch, the other EVE clients are muted. Starts at your next switch; turning it off unmutes them at once.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.muteNoneActive">Mute everything when no EVE client is in front</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.muteNoneActive.Desc">Instead of leaving the last client you played audible.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.clients.audio.volumes">Volume per client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.volume">Running clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.volume.Desc">Each client's volume in Windows. A client remembers it for next time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.clients.audio.volume.Empty">No clients are running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.audio.Intro">Hear only the client you're playing, and set each client's own volume.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.audio.solo.Title">Only the active client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.audio.solo.Body">With **Only hear the active client** on, switching mutes every other EVE client and unmutes the one you switch to. **Mute everything when no EVE client is in front** also mutes the last one when you go to another app.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.audio.volume.Title">Volume per client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.clients.audio.volume.Body">Each running client gets a slider. The volume is remembered per character and applied again when you switch to it. You can also set it from a thumbnail's right-click menu.</sys:String>

    <!-- Home -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.home">Home</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.home.Desc">The essentials: your clients, the keys to switch between them, thumbnails and combat alerts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.welcome">Simple mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.simpleBanner">You're in Simple mode: this page has what most players need. Every other setting is one click away.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.showAllRow">All settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.showAllRow.Desc">Shows every page in the navigation. Switch back with the switch at the bottom left.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.home.showAll">Show all settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.clients">Your clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.empty">No EVE clients are running</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.empty.Desc">Start EVE and log in: each character gets a tile here, with its hotkey and a thumbnail switch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Home.Show">Thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Home.GroupRow">{0} · {1} clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.switching">Switching</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.groupKeys">Group keys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.groupKeys.Desc">Each group in this profile switches through its own members.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.next">Next client, all running clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.next.Desc">Goes through every running client, whatever its group. Each tile above can have its own key too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.previous">Previous client, all running clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.thumbnails">Thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.size">Thumbnail size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.size.Desc">Width of every thumbnail; the height follows at 16:9. Drag a thumbnail's edge to size one on its own.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.opacity">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.opacity.Desc">Lower lets the game show through the thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.monitor">Monitor for new thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.monitor.Desc">Where thumbnails appear before you move them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Monitor.Item">Monitor {0}: {1}×{2}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Monitor.Primary">(primary)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.alerts">Combat alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertAttack">Under attack</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertAttack.Desc">A client is being shot at.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertScram">Warp scrambled</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertScram.Desc">A client can't warp away.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertDecloak">Decloaked</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertDecloak.Desc">A client's cloak dropped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertFleet">Fleet invite</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertFleet.Desc">A client was invited to a fleet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertSound">Play a sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.alertSound.Desc">Choose the sounds under Alerts › Sounds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.quick">Quick actions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.quick.hideAll">Hide all thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.quick.lock">Lock thumbnail positions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.quick.pause">Pause hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.quick.clickThrough">Click-through thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.home.startup">Startup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.startWithWindows">Start with Windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.home.startWithWindows.Desc">Launch MultiPreview to the tray when you sign in to Windows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.Intro">Everything to get going on one page: your clients, the keys to switch between them, how big the thumbnails are, and the alerts that matter in combat.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.clients.Title">Your clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.clients.Body">Each running character gets a tile. Click its key to record a hotkey that switches straight to it, and use the switch to hide or show its thumbnail. **›** opens every setting for that character.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.switching.Title">Switching clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.switching.Body">**Group keys** switch through one group's members, in its order: set them here or under Clients › Groups.&#x0A;**Next client** and **Previous client, all running clients** go through every running client. Hold a key to keep going.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.thumbnails.Title">Thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.thumbnails.Body">**Thumbnail size** sets every thumbnail at once and keeps a 16:9 shape. Drag a thumbnail to move it, or drag its edge to size just that one.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Opacity** lets the game show through. More looks are under Thumbnails in all settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.alerts.Title">Combat alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.alerts.Body">MultiPreview reads EVE's chat and combat logs and flashes the thumbnail of the client that needs you. Turn on the events you care about. Every other event, colours and sounds are under Alerts in all settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.quick.Title">Quick actions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.home.quick.Body">Each switch does the same as its hotkey, shown next to it: hide every thumbnail, lock them in place, pause all hotkeys, or let clicks go through the thumbnails.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Show all settings** opens every page, if you want more than the essentials.</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails › Appearance (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.appearance">Appearance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.appearance.Desc">Size, opacity, zoom and background for every thumbnail.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.appearance.size">Size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.resizeAll">Resize every thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.resizeAll.Desc">Width × height. Apply to all resizes every thumbnail where it is, and new thumbnails start at this size. Undo it under Layout &amp; screens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.appearance.applySize">Apply to all</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.individualResize">Resize thumbnails one at a time</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.individualResize.Desc">On: resizing a thumbnail changes only that one. Off: every thumbnail follows, unless you hold Ctrl.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.appearance.seeThrough">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.opacity">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.opacity.Desc">Lower lets the game behind show through. The same setting as on Home.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.opacityOnHover">Solid under the mouse</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.opacityOnHover.Desc">A thumbnail turns fully opaque while the mouse is over it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.appearance.zoom">Hover zoom</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.hoverZoom">Zoom under the mouse</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.hoverZoom.Desc">A thumbnail grows while the mouse rests on it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.hoverScale">Zoom size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.hoverScale.Desc">How big it grows, compared with its normal size.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.appearance.backdrop">Background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.background">Background colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.background.Desc">Fills a thumbnail where there is no picture.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.appearance.Intro">How every thumbnail looks: its size, how much of the game shows through it, the zoom under the mouse and the colour behind the picture. A character can also have its own size, set on its page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.appearance.size.Title">Sizing thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.appearance.size.Body">**Resize every thumbnail** gives all of them the same exact size at once, and new thumbnails start at it. Thumbnails stay where they are, and **Undo** (Layout &amp; screens) puts the old sizes back.&#x0A;&#x0A;To size by hand, hold the right mouse button on a thumbnail, press the left button too and drag. With **Resize thumbnails one at a time** off, every thumbnail follows; hold Ctrl to size just one.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Limit how small thumbnails get** sets the smallest size a drag can give. While it is off, that is 80 × 50.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.appearance.look.Title">Opacity, zoom and background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.appearance.look.Body">- **Opacity** lets the game behind show through. **Solid under the mouse** makes a thumbnail opaque while you point at it.&#x0A;- **Zoom under the mouse** enlarges a thumbnail while the mouse rests on it, to the **Zoom size** you pick.&#x0A;- **Background colour** fills a thumbnail where there is no picture.</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails Text and borders (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.text">Text &amp; borders</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.text.Desc">What each thumbnail shows on top of the picture, and the borders that tell clients apart.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.text.labels">Text on thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showText">Character name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showText.Desc">Each thumbnail shows its character's name.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showSystem">Solar system</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showSystem.Desc">The system each character is in, read from its EVE logs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showTimer">Session timer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showTimer.Desc">How long each client has been open.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.color">Text colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.color.Desc">Also used for crop window names.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.font">Font</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.font.Desc">The name of a font installed in Windows, like Segoe UI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.size">Text size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.marginX">Distance from the left edge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.marginY">Distance from the top edge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Err.FontName">Enter the name of a font, like Segoe UI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.text.stats">Client stats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showStats">CPU, memory and graphics use</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.showStats.Desc">Each client's CPU, RAM and VRAM use, updated every few seconds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.statsSize">Stats text size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.text.active">The client you're playing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlight">Highlight border</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlight.Desc">A coloured border marks the client in front. Changes show when you go back to EVE.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlightColor">Highlight colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlightWidth">Highlight width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlightInGroup">Keep the highlight inside a coloured group</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.highlightInGroup.Desc">With group borders on, the client you're playing keeps the highlight colour instead of its group's.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.text.others">Other clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.inactiveColor">Border colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.inactiveColor.Desc">Around every other thumbnail. Leave it empty for no border.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.inactiveWidth">Border width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.inactiveWidth.Desc">0 hides the border.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.groupBorders">Group colours</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.groupBorders.Desc">To paint each group member's border in its group's colour, turn on Show group borders on the Groups page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.text.openGroups">Open groups</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.text.marks">Marks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.badgePosition">Where the skipped-client mark goes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.text.badgePosition.Desc">A client taken out of cycling shows a red ✕ here.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorTopLeft">Top left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorTop">Top</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorTopRight">Top right</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorLeft">Left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorCenter">Centre</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorRight">Right</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorBottomLeft">Bottom left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorBottom">Bottom</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.AnchorBottomRight">Bottom right</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.Intro">What each thumbnail shows on top of the picture, and the borders that tell the client you're playing from the rest.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.text.Title">Text on thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.text.Body">Turn on the character name, the solar system (read from EVE's logs) and the session timer. **Text colour**, **Font** and **Text size** apply to all of them and to crop window names.&#x0A;&#x0A;A character's own label, with its own colour and size, is set on that character's page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.stats.Title">Client stats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.stats.Body">Shows how much CPU, memory (RAM) and graphics memory (VRAM) each client uses, updated every few seconds. Handy for spotting a client that's struggling.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.borders.Title">Borders</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.borders.Body">- The **highlight border** marks the client you're playing. Changes show when you go back to EVE.&#x0A;- Every other client gets the border under **Other clients**. Leave its colour empty for no border.&#x0A;- Groups can paint their members in the group colour (Clients › Groups). **Keep the highlight inside a coloured group** keeps the highlight colour on the client you're playing.&#x0A;- A character's own border colours are set on its page and used while **Use per-character colours** is on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.marks.Title">The skipped-client mark</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.text.marks.Body">A client you take out of cycling (Shift+click by default) shows a red ✕. Choose which corner or edge of the thumbnail it sits on.</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails › Layout &amp; screens (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.layout">Layout &amp; screens</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.layout.Desc">Where thumbnails appear, how they line up, saved layouts and undo.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.layout.screens">Screens</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.monitor">Monitor for new thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.monitor.Desc">Where thumbnails appear before you move them. The same setting as on Home.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.identifyRow">Which screen is which</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.identifyRow.Desc">Shows each monitor's number on it for a moment. MultiPreview's numbers can differ from Windows' display numbers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.layout.identify">Identify</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Monitor.Badge">Monitor {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.layout.newThumbnails">New thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startX">Distance from the screen's left edge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startX.Desc">Where a thumbnail with no saved place appears, on the monitor above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startY">Distance from the screen's top edge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startWidth">Starting width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startWidth.Desc">The size a new thumbnail starts at. Resize every thumbnail (Appearance) sets it too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.startHeight">Starting height</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.layout.lining">Lining up</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.snap">Snap to edges</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.snap.Desc">A thumbnail you let go of lines up with the edges of its neighbours and the screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.snapDistance">Snap distance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.snapDistance.Desc">How close an edge must be to snap.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.confine">Keep drags on one monitor</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.confine.Desc">A thumbnail you drag stays on the monitor it started on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.lock">Lock thumbnail positions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.lock.Desc">Thumbnails can't be moved or resized by dragging. Also a quick action on Home, and a hotkey.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.layout.undo">Undo and reset</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.history">Undo, redo and reset</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.history.Desc">Undo or redo moving or resizing every thumbnail at once, a saved layout or a reset.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.layout.undo">Undo</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.layout.redo">Redo</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.layout.reset">Reset all positions…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Layout.ResetTitle">Reset all positions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Layout.ResetConfirm">Put every thumbnail back in a column where new thumbnails appear, at the starting size? The places saved in this profile are cleared. You can undo it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.Intro">Where thumbnails appear and how they line up when you drag them, saved layouts you can put back in one click, and undo.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.screens.Title">Screens and new thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.screens.Body">A thumbnail with no saved place appears on the **monitor for new thumbnails**, at the distance and size under **New thumbnails**.&#x0A;&#x0A;Press **Identify** to see which screen has which number: MultiPreview's numbers can differ from Windows' display numbers.&#x0A;&#x0A;MultiPreview puts such thumbnails in a column, **Gap between thumbnails** apart, and starts a new column at the bottom of the screen. **Reset all positions** lays every thumbnail out that way.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.lining.Title">Moving thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.lining.Body">Hold the right mouse button on a thumbnail and drag to move it; hold Ctrl too to move them all.&#x0A;- **Snap to edges** lines a thumbnail up with its neighbours and the screen edge when you let go.&#x0A;- **Keep drags on one monitor** stops a thumbnail crossing to another screen.&#x0A;- **Lock thumbnail positions** stops all moving and resizing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.history.Title">Undo and reset</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.history.Body">**Undo** and **Redo** step back and forward through changes that moved or resized every thumbnail at once: dragging them all, resizing them all, a saved layout or a reset. They have hotkeys too (Clients › Hotkeys &amp; switching).&#x0A;&#x0A;**Reset all positions** puts every thumbnail back in a column at the place and size for new thumbnails, and clears the places saved in this profile.</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails › Layout &amp; screens › Saved layouts (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.layout.saved">Saved layouts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.presets">Your layouts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.presets.Desc">Save where every thumbnail is and how big, then put them back in one click (layout presets). Shared by every profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Apply">Apply</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Remap">Remap and apply…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Delete">Delete…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Save">Save current layout…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Export">Export…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Import">Import…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Empty">No saved layouts yet. Place your thumbnails, then save the layout.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.NoneUsed">This profile hasn't used a saved layout yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Current">This profile last used: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.PickFirst">Pick a saved layout first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Applied">Layout '{0}' applied.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.NoClients">No clients are running to place.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.NoThumbnails">There are no thumbnails to save. Start your clients first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.SaveTitle">Save layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.NamePrompt">Name for this layout:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.ReplaceTitle">Replace layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.ReplaceConfirm">A layout called '{0}' already exists. Replace it?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Saved">Layout '{0}' saved.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.DeleteTitle">Delete layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.DeleteConfirm">Delete the saved layout '{0}'?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Exported">Saved as {0}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.ExportFailed">Couldn't write that file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.Imported">Layout '{0}' imported.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Presets.ImportFailed">That file isn't a MultiPreview layout.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Filter.Layouts">MultiPreview layouts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.presets.Title">Saved layouts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.layout.presets.Body">**Save current layout** remembers where every running character's thumbnail is and how big, as a share of its screen, so the layout still fits after a resolution change. It also remembers which thumbnails are hidden and whether crop windows are on.&#x0A;- **Apply** puts the thumbnails back. Characters that aren't logged in get their place when they log in.&#x0A;- **Remap and apply** lets you choose which of your characters takes each place, for example in a layout from another player.&#x0A;- **Export** and **Import** share a layout as a file. Importing a layout with the name of one you already have asks before it replaces it.</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails › Visibility (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.visibility">Visibility</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.visibility.Desc">When thumbnails stay on top or get out of the way, the login-screen mark, and second thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.visibility.stacking">Staying on top</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.alwaysOnTop">Always on top</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.alwaysOnTop.Desc">Thumbnails stay above every other window, your browser included.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.aboveClients">Keep above EVE clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.aboveClients.Desc">While you play, thumbnails stay above your EVE clients but other apps can cover them. Meant for use with Always on top off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.visibility.hiding">When to hide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.hideOnLostFocus">Hide when you switch to another app</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.hideOnLostFocus.Desc">Thumbnails disappear while no EVE client is in front and come back when one is. They stay while settings is open.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.hideActive">Hide the client you're playing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.hideActive.Desc">Only the thumbnail of the client in front hides.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.visibility.login">Clients at the login screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.notLoggedIn">Mark for a client not logged in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.notLoggedIn.Desc">How a thumbnail shows a client still at character selection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.NotLoggedInNone">Nothing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.NotLoggedInText">“Not logged in” text</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.NotLoggedInBorder">Coloured border</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.NotLoggedInDim">Dimmed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.notLoggedInColor">Border colour for clients not logged in</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.visibility.pip">Second thumbnails (PiP)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.pipTable">Second thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.visibility.pipTable.Desc">An extra thumbnail of the same client with its own place, size and opacity. Off keeps its place and size for next time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.ColOn">On</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.ColOpacity">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.Empty">No second thumbnails yet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.Add">Add…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.AddTitle">Add a second thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.AddExists">'{0}' already has a second thumbnail.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.Remove">Remove…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.OnFor">Second thumbnail for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.OpacityFor">Second thumbnail opacity for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.RemoveFor">Remove {0}'s second thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.RemoveTitle">Remove second thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Pip.RemoveConfirm">Remove {0}'s second thumbnail? Its place and size are forgotten. To keep them, turn it off instead.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.Intro">When thumbnails stay above other windows or get out of the way, how a client still at the login screen looks, and second thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.stacking.Title">Staying on top and hiding</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.stacking.Body">- **Always on top** keeps thumbnails above every window, your browser included.&#x0A;- **Keep above EVE clients** keeps them above EVE while you play but lets other apps cover them. Use it with Always on top off.&#x0A;- **Hide when you switch to another app** clears them away while no EVE client is in front.&#x0A;- **Hide the client you're playing** hides only the thumbnail of the client in front, since you're already looking at it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.login.Title">Clients at the login screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.login.Body">A client still at character selection can show **“Not logged in”** text, a **coloured border**, or be **dimmed**, so you can see which clients still need logging in.&#x0A;&#x0A;The text is drawn under the live picture, so it shows only while thumbnails are partly see-through (Appearance › Opacity).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.pip.Title">Second thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.visibility.pip.Body">A second thumbnail is an extra view of a client with its own place, size and opacity, for example a large view of your main next to the wall.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Add** picks a character; drag the second thumbnail like any other. Turning it off keeps its place and size for next time, while **Remove** forgets them. Each character's page has the same switch, and a hotkey can hide every second thumbnail (Clients › Hotkeys &amp; switching).</sys:String>
    <!-- Thumbnails › Crop windows (Plan 3b) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.crops">Crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.thumbs.crops.Desc">Small windows that each show one part of a client, like its overview or local chat.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.crops.master">Crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.crops.enabled">Show crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.crops.enabled.Desc">Off hides every crop window and keeps it for next time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.crops.off">Crop windows are off. You can still set them up here; they appear when you turn them on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.thumbs.crops.list">Your crop windows</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.crops.editor">Character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.crops.editor.Desc">Whose crop windows to edit. Every character MultiPreview knows is listed, running ones first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.thumbs.crops.add">Add a crop window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.NoCharacters">No characters yet. Start EVE and log in first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Empty">{0} has no crop windows yet. Add one, then press Edit area while the client is running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.DefaultName">Crop {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Name">Name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.ShowName">Show the name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.EditArea">Edit area…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.CopyTo">Copy to…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Delete">Delete…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Area">Part of the client</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Window">Window on screen</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Opacity">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.ClickThrough">Clicks pass through</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Tip">Drag a crop window with the right mouse button to move it; press the left button too to resize it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.CopyAll">All other characters ({0})</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.CopyNone">No other characters</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.Copied">Copied '{0}' to {1}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.CopiedMany">Copied '{0}' to {1} characters.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.DeleteTitle">Delete crop window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.DeleteConfirm">Delete the crop window '{0}'?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.NeedsClient">Start {0}'s client first: the area is picked on the running client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.NoClientArea">Couldn't read {0}'s window. Make sure it isn't minimized.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Crops.PickFailed">The area picker couldn't open. Try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.crops.Intro">A crop window shows one part of a client, such as its overview, local chat or a row of modules, in its own small window you can put anywhere.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.crops.crops.Title">Making a crop window</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.crops.crops.Body">- Pick a character and press **Add a crop window**.&#x0A;- With that client running, press **Edit area** and drag over the part you want. The window takes the same size.&#x0A;- Drag a crop window with the right mouse button to move it; press the left button too to resize it.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Copy to** gives other characters the same crop window, at the same place on screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.crops.options.Title">Opacity, clicks and turning them off</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.thumbs.crops.options.Body">**Opacity** lets what's behind show through. With **Clicks pass through** on, your clicks reach the window behind, and the crop window can't be dragged.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Show crop windows** off hides them all and keeps them for next time. A hotkey can hide them too (Clients › Hotkeys &amp; switching).</sys:String>
    <!-- Alerts › Events (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.events">Events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.events.Desc">What MultiPreview watches for in EVE's logs, and how each alert shows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.events.logs">Reading EVE's logs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.chatLog">Read chat logs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.chatLog.Desc">Tells MultiPreview which system each client is in: system-change alerts and the system name on thumbnails.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.chatFolder">Chat log folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.chatFolder.Desc">Leave empty for EVE's usual folder, Documents\EVE\logs\Chatlogs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.gameLog">Read game logs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.gameLog.Desc">Needed for every other alert and for the stats overlay.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.gameFolder">Game log folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.gameFolder.Desc">Leave empty for EVE's usual folder, Documents\EVE\logs\Gamelogs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.events.combat">Combat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.pve">PVE mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.pve.Desc">NPCs shooting or scrambling you don't raise an alert; players still do. NPC damage still counts in the stats overlay unless you turn that off (Tools › Stats overlay).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.underFire">Under-fire border</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.underFire.Desc">A thumbnail pulses red while that client takes damage, from players or NPCs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.underFireTime">Under-fire border lasts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.underFireTime.Desc">Seconds after the last hit before the border goes.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.events.repeats">Repeats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.repeatWait">Quiet time before an alert repeats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.repeatWait.Desc">After an alert fires for a character, the same alert stays quiet for this many seconds. 0 = never quiet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.events.list">Events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.table">Alert events</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.table.Desc">Turn each event on or off and choose how its alert shows on the thumbnail.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColEvent">Event</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColSeverity">Severity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColColour">Colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColLasts">Lasts (s)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColBadge">Badge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColSteady">Steady</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ColOn">On</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.Group.combat">Combat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.Group.fleet">Fleet and chat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.Group.travel">Travel</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.Group.mining">Mining</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sev.critical">Critical</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sev.warning">Warning</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sev.info">Info</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.Note">Lasts: empty uses the severity's time (critical 8 s, warning 6 s, info 4 s); 0 keeps the alert until you switch to that client. Badge needs the count badge on (Look &amp; severity). Info alerts are always steady.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.LastsError">Enter seconds from {0} to {1}, or leave it empty for the severity's time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.PickColour">Pick a colour for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.ResetColour">Use the severity colour for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.LastsFor">How long {0} lasts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.BadgeFor">Badge for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.SteadyFor">Steady border for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.OnFor">{0} on</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Events.InfoSteady">Info alerts are always steady.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Unit.Sec">s</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.Intro">MultiPreview reads the log files EVE writes for each client and raises an alert when something happens: you're shot at, scrambled, invited, a rock runs dry. An alert flashes that client's thumbnail and can also badge it, write what happened on it, play a sound and show a toast.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.logs.Title">Where alerts come from</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.logs.Body">- **Chat logs** tell MultiPreview which system each client is in.&#x0A;- **Game logs** carry combat, fleet, conversation and mining lines, and feed the stats overlay.&#x0A;&#x0A;Both are on by default and read from EVE's usual folders. Change a folder only if you moved EVE's logs. A change applies at once, and reading carries on where it was, so no alert shows twice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.combat.Title">PVE mode and the under-fire border</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.combat.Body">**PVE mode** is for ratting and missions: NPCs shooting or scrambling you no longer raise an alert, players still do.&#x0A;&#x0A;The **under-fire border** pulses red on a thumbnail while that client takes damage, and goes a few seconds after the last hit.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.table.Title">The event table</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.events.table.Body">Each row is one kind of alert.&#x0A;- **Severity** is fixed for each event. It gives the event its colour, flash speed and toast choice (Look &amp; severity).&#x0A;- **Colour** gives one event its own colour; ↺ goes back to the severity's.&#x0A;- **Lasts** is how long the alert stays on the thumbnail.&#x0A;- **Badge** counts the event on the thumbnail; **Steady** holds the border instead of blinking.&#x0A;- **On** turns the event off completely.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Quiet time** stops the same alert repeating for a character for a few seconds. **Quiet time per severity** (Look &amp; severity) gives each severity its own.</sys:String>
    <!-- Alerts › Look & severity (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.look">Look &amp; severity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.look.Desc">How alerts look on thumbnails, the three severities, and colour-blind mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.look.thumbnail">On the thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.pulse">Pulse strength</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.pulse.Desc">How solid the alert colour is. Lower is softer, which helps with many clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.borderWidth">Alert border width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.borderWidth.Desc">The band that flashes just inside the thumbnail's border. 0 = no band.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.badge">Count badge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.badge.Desc">A small number in the thumbnail's corner counts alerts until you switch to that client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.text">Write what happened</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.text.Desc">Shows the event, such as "Warp scrambled", on the thumbnail while the alert lasts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.textPosition">Text position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.textPosition.Desc">Where that text sits on the thumbnail.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.look.severity">Severities</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.severityTable">Severity settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.severityTable.Desc">Every event is critical, warning or info. These apply to every event of that severity.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.ColSeverity">Severity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.ColColour">Colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.ColFlash">Flash speed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.ColHub">Toast in the alert hub</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.InfoSteady">Always steady</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.Note">The colour is used by every event without its own colour (Events). Flash speed is how fast the border blinks: lower is faster. Toasts show only while the alert hub is on (Alert hub).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.PickColour">Pick a colour for {0} alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.FlashFor">Flash speed for {0} alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Severity.HubFor">Toast for {0} alerts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.look.accessibility">Accessibility</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.colorBlind">Colour-blind mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.colorBlind.Desc">Colours colour-blind players can tell apart, for alerts, the highlight border, thumbnail text, the login mark and the stats overlay. Turning it off gives your own colours back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.ColorBlind.ConfirmOn">Turn on colour-blind mode? It replaces your alert, highlight, thumbnail text, login mark and stats colours with a colour-blind-safe set, and removes the colours you gave single events. Turning it off later gives your colours back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.ColorBlind.ConfirmOff">Turn off colour-blind mode? It sets the standard alert, highlight, thumbnail text, login mark and stats colours. Colours you had before turning it on don't come back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.Intro">How an alert looks on a thumbnail. Severity settings apply to every event of that severity; a single event can still have its own colour on the Events page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.thumbnail.Title">On the thumbnail</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.thumbnail.Body">An alert flashes a band just inside the thumbnail's border, so you can still see which client is active.&#x0A;- **Pulse strength** softens the colour; **Alert border width** sets the band (0 turns it off).&#x0A;- The **count badge** counts alerts until you switch to that client.&#x0A;- **Write what happened** puts the event's name on the thumbnail in the alert's colour.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.severity.Title">Severities</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.severity.Body">Every event is **critical**, **warning** or **info**. Each severity has a colour, a flash speed and a choice of whether its alerts show a toast in the alert hub. Info alerts don't blink: they stay steady.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.colorBlind.Title">Colour-blind mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.colorBlind.Body">Colour-blind mode switches to the Wong palette, colours that stay distinct for every kind of colour blindness. It replaces the alert, highlight, thumbnail text, login mark and stats colours and removes per-event colours, so it asks first. Turning it off gives back the colours you had before. If it was turned on in an older version of MultiPreview, turning it off sets the standard colours.</sys:String>
    <!-- Alerts › Sounds and Alert hub (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.sounds">Sounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.sounds.Desc">One sound for every alert, or a different one for each event.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.sounds.main">Sounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.enabled">Play alert sounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.enabled.Desc">The same switch as Play a sound on Home.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.volume">Volume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.volume.Desc">For alert sounds and the wrap-around sound.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.sounds.list">Sound files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.table">Sound for each event</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.sounds.table.Desc">WAV or MP3 files. An event without its own sound plays the default sound.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.ColEvent">Event</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.ColSound">Sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.ColWait">Wait (s)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Default">Default sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.UsesDefault">Default sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.None">No sound</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Change">Change…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Play">Play</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Clear">Clear</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.ChangeFor">Change the sound for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.PlayFor">Play the sound for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.ClearFor">Clear the sound for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.WaitFor">Seconds before {0} plays again</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Missing">There's no sound to play, or its file can't be found.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.WaitError">Enter seconds from {0} to {1}. Empty or 0 = no wait.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sounds.Note">Wait: after a sound plays for a character, that event's sound stays silent for this many seconds. Empty or 0 = no wait (the quiet time on Events still applies). Play uses the volume above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.sounds.Intro">Alerts can play a sound. Pick one default sound for every event, then give some events their own.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.sounds.sounds.Title">Choosing sounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.sounds.sounds.Body">- **Change…** picks a WAV or MP3 file; **Play** tries it at the volume above; **Clear** goes back to the default sound.&#x0A;- An event with no sound of its own and no default sound is silent.&#x0A;- **Wait** stops the same event's sound repeating for one character, for example a rock running dry on every miner.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.hub">Alert hub</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.alerts.hub.Desc">A small floating icon that collects alerts as toasts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.hub.main">Alert hub</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.enabled">Show the alert hub</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.enabled.Desc">Drag it with the mouse; right-click it to choose where toasts stack.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.duration">Toasts last</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.duration.Desc">Seconds before a toast goes by itself. Click a toast to switch to that client.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.direction">Toasts stack</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.direction.Desc">Which side of the hub new toasts appear on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.DirUp">Up</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.DirRight">Right</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.DirDown">Down</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Opt.DirLeft">Left</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.skipActive">No toast for the client you're playing</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.skipActive.Desc">You're already looking at it. Its thumbnail still flashes and its sound still plays.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.hub.hiding">Hiding and position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.autoHide">Hide when quiet</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.autoHide.Desc">The hub disappears after a quiet spell and comes back with the next alert.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.autoHideAfter">Hide after</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.autoHideAfter.Desc">Seconds without a new alert.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.positionRow">Hub position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.positionRow.Desc">Moves the hub back to the right edge of the main screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.alerts.hub.resetPosition">Reset position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.AlertHub.ResetDone">The alert hub is back at the right edge of the main screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.Intro">The alert hub is a small icon that stays on top of EVE. Each alert can show a toast beside it, naming the client and the event.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.hub.Title">Toasts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.hub.Body">Which severities show a toast is set under Look &amp; severity. Click a toast to switch to that client; click the hub to clear them all. Drag the hub anywhere, and right-click it to choose the side toasts stack on.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.hiding.Title">Hiding the hub</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.hiding.Body">**Hide when quiet** keeps the hub out of the way until an alert arrives. If you lose the hub off screen, **Reset position** brings it back.</sys:String>
    <!-- Performance (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.cpu">CPU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.cpu.Desc">Give the client you're playing the processor, and keep the others on less.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.cpu.priority">Background clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.manage">Manage background priority</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.manage.Desc">Clients you aren't playing run at low priority. The one in front gets normal priority and every core. For this profile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.autoBalance">Spread background clients over the last cores</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.autoBalance.Desc">Each background client gets one core from the second half of your cores (the efficiency cores on most Intel processors). A pinned core below wins.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.cpu.pins">Pinned cores</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.coreTable">Core for each character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.cpu.coreTable.Desc">The core a character's client uses while it's in the background. Automatic follows the switch above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.CoreTable.ColCore">Core in the background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.CoreTable.Empty">No characters yet. Start EVE and log in, or add characters on Clients › Characters.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.CoreTable.CoreFor">Core for {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.cpu.Intro">With many clients, the one you're playing should get the processor. MultiPreview can lower the others and keep each one on a core.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.cpu.priority.Title">Background priority and cores</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.cpu.priority.Body">With **Manage background priority** on, every client you aren't playing runs at low priority; the one in front runs normally on every core. Turning it off gives every client its normal priority and all cores back.&#x0A;- **Spread background clients over the last cores** gives each one a core from the second half of your cores.&#x0A;- A **pinned core** keeps one character on the core you choose. The character's own page has the same setting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.gpu">GPU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.gpu.Desc">Save graphics power when you run many clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.gpu.preset">Quick setup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.presetRow">Low-GPU setup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.presetRow.Desc">Turns on two settings: minimize clients when you switch away (Clients › Windows &amp; positions) and freeze thumbnails while you're in another app.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.perf.gpu.lowGpu">Use the low-GPU setup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.LowGpuDone">Low-GPU setup on. Tip: set a frame rate limit and vsync in each EVE client too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.gpu.thumbnails">Thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.static">Still thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.static.Desc">Thumbnails show a snapshot once a second instead of live video. A big saving with many clients.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.suspend">Freeze thumbnails in the background</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.gpu.suspend.Desc">While neither EVE nor MultiPreview is in front, thumbnails keep their last picture. They go live again when you come back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.gpu.Intro">Every live thumbnail costs graphics power. These settings cut that cost, at the price of less motion.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.gpu.gpu.Title">Saving GPU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.gpu.gpu.Body">- **Still thumbnails** trades smooth motion for a big saving, all the time.&#x0A;- **Freeze thumbnails in the background** costs nothing while you play and saves while you're in another app.&#x0A;- **Use the low-GPU setup** turns on that freeze and minimizes clients you switch away from, so they stop drawing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.fps">FPS limiter</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.perf.fps.Desc">Hold background clients to a low frame rate with RivaTuner Statistics Server, and show each client's FPS.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.fps.rtss">RivaTuner Statistics Server</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.rtssMissing">RivaTuner Statistics Server (RTSS) isn't installed. The frame limit and the FPS counter need it; it comes with MSI Afterburner, or on its own.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.rtssFound">RivaTuner Statistics Server (RTSS) is installed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.fps.limit">Frame limit</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.background">Background frame rate</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.background.Desc">The frame rate EVE clients drop to while they aren't in front. Apply it to RTSS with the button below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.applyRow">RTSS profile</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.applyRow.Desc">Writes an EVE profile into RTSS and restarts it. Windows may ask for permission.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.perf.fps.apply">Apply to RTSS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.RtssApplied">The RTSS profile is in place. Background clients now drop to the chosen frame rate.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.RtssFailed">Couldn't apply the RTSS profile: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.fps.counter">FPS counter</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.show">Show each client's FPS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.show.Desc">Writes the frame rate RTSS reports in the top right corner of every thumbnail.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.insetX">Distance from the right edge</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.insetX.Desc">-1 = the standard 5 px.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.insetY">Distance from the top</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.insetY.Desc">-1 = the same as the thumbnail text's top margin.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.size">Text size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.size.Desc">0 = the same size as the thumbnail text.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.perf.fps.manual">Install by hand</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.target">If Apply to RTSS can't write the profile, copy the file and paste it into {0}, then restart RTSS.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.manualRow">Profile file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.perf.fps.manualRow.Desc">Copy puts the file on the clipboard, ready to paste in File Explorer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.perf.fps.copyFile">Copy the file</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Act.perf.fps.openFolder">Open the folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.NoRtssFolder">(RTSS isn't installed)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.FileCopied">Profile file copied. Paste it into {0}, then restart RTSS.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.CopyFailed">Couldn't copy the profile file. Try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.NoRtss">RTSS isn't installed, so there's no folder to open.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Perf.OpenFailed">Couldn't open the folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.Intro">RivaTuner Statistics Server (RTSS) can hold EVE clients you aren't playing to a low frame rate, which saves a lot of GPU and power. MultiPreview writes the RTSS profile for you and can show each client's FPS.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.limit.Title">Limiting background clients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.limit.Body">Choose a **background frame rate**, then press **Apply to RTSS**. The profile limits EVE only while it's in the background, so the client you play keeps its full frame rate. RTSS restarts to load it, and Windows may ask for permission.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.counter.Title">The FPS counter</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.counter.Body">With RTSS running, each thumbnail can show its client's frame rate in the top right corner. Move it with the two distances, or change its size; -1 and 0 keep the standard place and size.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.manual.Title">Installing the profile by hand</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.perf.fps.manual.Body">If Windows refuses permission, press **Copy the file**, then **Open the folder**, paste the file there and restart RTSS.</sys:String>
    <!-- Tools › Stats overlay (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.tools.stats">Stats overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Page.tools.stats.Desc">Live numbers next to each thumbnail: damage, repairs, mining and ISK.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.tools.stats.overlay">Overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.enabled">Show the stats overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.enabled.Desc">A small window per character with the numbers chosen below. Drag it with the right mouse button.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.hideOnLostFocus">Hide when you switch to another app</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.hideOnLostFocus.Desc">Stats windows hide while neither EVE nor MultiPreview is in front.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.tools.stats.numbers">Numbers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.metrics">Numbers for every character</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.metrics.Desc">A character shows these unless its own page says otherwise. The numbers come from EVE's game logs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.DpsOut">Damage dealt per second (Out)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.DpsIn">Damage taken per second (In)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tdi">Total damage taken (TDI)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tdo">Total damage dealt (TDO)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.DpsInByType">Damage taken by type (EM, Th, Ki, Ex %)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Arps">Armour repaired per second (ARPS)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Srps">Shield repaired per second (SRPS)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Ctps">Capacitor sent per second (CTPS)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Taro">Total armour repairs given (TARO)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tari">Total armour repairs received (TARI)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tsro">Total shield repairs given (TSRO)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tsri">Total shield repairs received (TSRI)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Ompc">Ore per cycle (OMPC)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Omph">Ore per hour (OMPH)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Gmpc">Gas per cycle (GMPC)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Gmph">Gas per hour (GMPH)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Imph">Ice per hour (IMPH)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tipt">ISK per bounty tick (TIPT)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tiph">ISK per hour (TIPH)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Stat.Tips">ISK this session (TIPS)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.tools.stats.look">Look</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.fontSize">Text size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.fontSize.Desc">The size of the numbers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.opacity">Opacity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.opacity.Desc">Lower lets the game behind show through.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.background">Background colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.background.Desc">Behind the numbers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.textColor">Text colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.textColor.Desc">The colour of the numbers. Colour-blind mode replaces it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.tools.stats.logging">Logging</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.csv">Save stats to CSV files</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.csv.Desc">One file per character per day, for a spreadsheet.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.logFolder">Log folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.logFolder.Desc">Where the files go. It's made if it doesn't exist.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.noFolder">Choose a log folder: without one nothing is saved.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.keepDays">Keep files for</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.keepDays.Desc">Older stats files in the folder are deleted when MultiPreview starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.keepZero">Keep files for is 0 days or less, so no stats file is ever deleted. Enter a number of days to delete older files.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Unit.Days">days</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.Intro">The stats overlay puts live numbers beside each client: damage per second, repairs, ore mined, ISK earned. They come from EVE's game logs, so game logs must be read (Alerts › Events).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.overlay.Title">The overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.overlay.Body">Each character with numbers to show gets a small window. Drag it with the right mouse button; press the left button too to resize it. **Hide when you switch to another app** keeps the windows out of the way while you're not in EVE.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.numbers.Title">Choosing numbers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.numbers.Body">The numbers here are for every character. A character can turn single numbers or whole groups on or off on its own page (Clients › Characters › the character). The short code in brackets is what the overlay writes.&#x0A;&#x0A;**Count NPC damage** decides whether hits from and on NPCs count in the damage numbers. It stays on unless you turn it off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.look.Title">Look</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.look.Body">Text size, opacity and the two colours apply to every stats window. Colours can be typed as #RRGGBB or picked with the swatch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.logging.Title">Saving stats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.tools.stats.logging.Body">With **Save stats to CSV files** on, MultiPreview writes one file per character per day into the log folder, for a spreadsheet. Files older than the keep time are deleted when MultiPreview starts; 0 days keeps every file. Turning logging on or off applies at once; a new keep time applies from the next start.</sys:String>
    <!-- Character page › Choose numbers, Tools › Stats overlay › Per character (Plan 3c) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.statsPicker">Choose numbers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.statsPicker.Desc">Show or hide single numbers for this character. Default follows the numbers for every character (Tools › Stats overlay).</sys:String>
