    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.look.repeats">Repeats</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.waitBySeverity">Quiet time per severity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.waitBySeverity.Desc">On: critical, warning and info alerts each wait their own time before the same alert shows again for a character. Off: every alert waits the quiet time on the Events page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.waitCritical">Critical alerts stay quiet for</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.waitWarning">Warning alerts stay quiet for</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.look.waitInfo">Info alerts stay quiet for</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.events.repeatBySeverity">Each severity has its own quiet time: Alerts › Look &amp; severity.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.repeats.Title">Quiet time per severity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.look.repeats.Body">An alert that just fired for a character stays quiet for a while, so a fight doesn't flood you with the same alert.&#x0A;- With **Quiet time per severity** off, every alert waits the quiet time on the Events page (5 seconds unless you changed it).&#x0A;- Turned on, critical, warning and info alerts each wait their own time, for example 2 seconds for critical and 60 for info. Each starts at 5 seconds, whatever quiet time the Events page has, so turning it on can change how long alerts wait until you set your own numbers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.minSizeOn">Limit how small thumbnails get</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.minSizeOn.Desc">Off: resizing a thumbnail by hand stops at 80 × 50. On: it stops at the size below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.minWidth">Smallest width</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.appearance.minHeight">Smallest height</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.gap">Gap between thumbnails</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.thumbs.layout.gap.Desc">The space MultiPreview leaves between the thumbnails it places itself: clients with no saved place, and Reset all positions.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.countNpc">Count NPC damage</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.tools.stats.countNpc.Desc">Off: hits from and on NPCs stay out of the damage numbers, so they show fights with players only. ISK from ratting still counts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.colorText">Text colour</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.character.colorText.Desc">Colours the text on this character's thumbnail. Until you pick one, it is the text colour from Thumbnails › Text &amp; borders.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.ColorBlind.ConfirmOffRestore">Turn off colour-blind mode? Your alert, highlight, thumbnail text, login mark and stats colours, and the colours you gave single events, go back to what they were before you turned it on.</sys:String>
