    <sys:String x:Key="L.Start.Restore.BesideExe">the settings file beside MultiPreview.exe</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Start.Restore.Backup">a saved copy in the Backups folder</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Start.Restore.Failed">That copy couldn't be restored. Pick another.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Move.Note">EVE MultiPreview now keeps its settings in this folder:&#x0A;{0}&#x0A;&#x0A;The settings file here, beside MultiPreview.exe, is the copy from before version {2}. MultiPreview doesn't use it any more, apart from the older-version case below, and you can keep it as a backup. If the settings file above ever goes missing, MultiPreview asks on the next start which copy to restore: one of its newer backups, or this file. If it has no newer backup, it copies this file back without asking.&#x0A;&#x0A;To keep everything beside the exe instead (a portable install, for example on a USB stick): close MultiPreview, copy the settings file (and layout_presets.json, if you use layout presets) from the folder above into this folder, and create an empty file named {1} here. MultiPreview then reads and saves its files here, as before.&#x0A;&#x0A;If you install an older version from Settings › App settings › About &amp; updates, MultiPreview first copies your current settings and layout presets here, because older versions read the files beside the exe. The files that were here are kept in the Backups folder inside the folder above.</sys:String>
