    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.Sec.alerts.hub.history">History</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.keepHistory">Keep an alert history</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.keepHistory.Desc">Every alert is added to a list on this PC: when, which character, which alert and where. Off adds nothing new.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.historyDays">Keep alerts for</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.historyDays.Desc">Older days are deleted when MultiPreview starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.S.alerts.hub.historyFolder">The history stays on this PC, in {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.history.Title">Alert history</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help.alerts.hub.history.Body">MultiPreview keeps a list of every alert that fires: the time, the character, the alert, its severity, the solar system, and whether it was shown or the character was muted. An alert you switched off isn't listed, and neither is a repeat inside the quiet time.&#x0A;&#x0A;- The list is one file per day in the History folder of your settings folder. MultiPreview keeps it there and sends it nowhere. A CSV file you export from the history window goes where you save it, and holds the same text.&#x0A;- For an alert of one of your own rules, the list also holds the rule's name and the line the rule matched, cut to 160 characters. A line of the game log can name other players, and in a chat channel the line is something another player wrote.&#x0A;- **Keep alerts for** sets how many days stay, 30 unless you change it. Older days are deleted the next time MultiPreview starts.&#x0A;- With **Keep an alert history** off, nothing new is written. What is already kept stays until its days run out or you clear it.</sys:String>
